modes/deliver-mode.md 76 - For delivery discrepancies, Apply [Read Delivery Evidence](../artifacts/delivery-evidence.md#read-delivery-evidence "ƒ") for the selected repositories and initiative against current issue records, then repeat this survey with its refreshed evidence before selecting a dispatch batch.
modes/deliver-mode.md 248 - Apply [Read Pull Request State](../artifacts/pull-request.md#read-pull-request-state "ƒ") with the same identity before selecting restoration.
modes/revise-mode.md 11 Read the [shared skill guidelines](../../guidelines.md) and [skill guidelines](../guidelines.md) whole before the first edit.
modes/sync-mode.md 13 - Apply [Read Tracker Issue](../artifacts/issue.md#read-tracker-issue "ƒ") for each selected issue before inspecting its Open Questions or format.
modes/sync-mode.md 246 - Apply [Read Tracker Issue](../artifacts/issue.md#read-tracker-issue "ƒ") for the originating proposal identified in the initiative's [References](../artifacts/initiative-issue-body.md#references); provide unresolved provenance before board creation for a proposal-derived initiative.
protocols/epic-integration.md 12 - For any failed preparation or readiness gate before a classified merge outcome, Apply [Hold Epic Review](../artifacts/pull-request.md#hold-epic-review "ƒ") and Apply [Record Epic Review](../artifacts/board-delivery.md#record-epic-review "ƒ") again with their preceding inputs before returning or retrying, including failures between ready and board writes. The confirmed absence of a board is the sole exception to board withdrawal.
protocols/epic-integration.md 46 - Apply [Fetch Merge Readiness](../artifacts/pull-request.md#fetch-merge-readiness "ƒ") for the exact current head and target. A conflict, failed or pending check, unmet epic condition or incomplete evidence blocks handoff; Apply [Hold Epic Review](../artifacts/pull-request.md#hold-epic-review "ƒ") again and Apply [Record Epic Review](../artifacts/board-delivery.md#record-epic-review "ƒ") requesting In Progress before returning that blocker. Pending required human approval is provided to the next step as a human handoff, with merge blocked.
protocols/unit-dispatch.md 22 - For a new unit of rows, read each component from the work-item file its free row links, before reservation replaces that link.
protocols/unit-dispatch.md 31 - Apply [Read Board State](../artifacts/board.md#read-board-state "ƒ") for the selected board immediately before acquiring the unit's hold.
rules.md 4   Read a heading-linked section and its subsections, stopping before the next heading of equal or higher level. Follow in-text links as their context is needed for the selected work. Preserve boundaries in batched reads and recover truncated output. Reuse complete context already read at the same revision. Explicit whole-document requirements still apply.
